@startuml
title Login With Google Sequence (/api/auth/google)
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor Guest
boundary "LoginScreen UI" as LoginScreen
control "GoogleAuthService" as GoogleAuthService
entity "GoogleLoginRequest\n(BE Request DTO)" as GoogleLoginRequestDto
entity "TokenResponse\n(BE Response DTO)" as GoogleLoginResponseDto
entity "AuthTokensDto\n(FE Response DTO)" as FeTokensDto
control "AuthController" as AuthController
control "IAuthService" as IAuthService
control "AuthService" as AuthService
entity "User" as UserEntity
entity "UserAuth" as UserAuthEntity
entity "UserProfile" as UserProfileEntity
entity "Role" as RoleEntity
entity "RefreshToken" as RefreshTokenEntity
control "IAuthAccountRepository" as IAuthAccountRepository
control "AuthAccountRepository" as AuthAccountRepository
database "VocaNovaDbContext" as DbContext
database "MySQL Database" as MySQL
note over LoginScreen, MySQL
BE DTOs exist: GoogleLoginRequest and TokenResponse.
FE response DTO exists: AuthTokensDto.
Mobile GoogleAuthService gets the id_token before the API call.
Interfaces used in code: IAuthService, IAuthAccountRepository.
end note
Guest -> LoginScreen: Access login page
Guest -> LoginScreen: Click Login with Google
LoginScreen -> GoogleAuthService: getIdToken()
GoogleAuthService --> LoginScreen: id_token
alt Google login cancelled or token missing
LoginScreen --> Guest: Show error message
else Google token received
LoginScreen -> GoogleLoginRequestDto: Create request data(id_token)
LoginScreen -> AuthController: POST /api/auth/googleGoogleLoginRequest
AuthController -> AuthController: Validate GoogleLoginRequest
alt Request validation or rate limit fails
AuthController --> LoginScreen: HTTP 400/429 error
LoginScreen --> Guest: Show error message
else Request validation success
AuthController -> IAuthService: GoogleLoginAsync(login data)
IAuthService -> AuthService: GoogleLoginAsync(login data)
AuthService -> IAuthService: Verify id_token
IAuthService -> AuthService: Verify id_token
alt id_token invalid
AuthService --> AuthController: Unauthorized result
AuthController --> LoginScreen: HTTP 401 Invalid Google id token
LoginScreen --> Guest: Show error message
else id_token valid
AuthService -> IAuthAccountRepository: FindByGoogleSubjectAsync(subject)
IAuthAccountRepository -> AuthAccountRepository: FindByGoogleSubjectAsync(subject)
AuthAccountRepository -> DbContext: Query user by Google subject
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT user account
MySQL --> DbContext: User row or null
DbContext -> UserEntity: Materialize User?
DbContext -> UserAuthEntity: Materialize UserAuth?
UserEntity --> DbContext: User or null
UserAuthEntity --> DbContext: UserAuth or null
DbContext --> AuthAccountRepository: Result
AuthAccountRepository --> AuthService: AuthAccount or null
alt Existing Google account
alt Account locked or deleted
AuthService --> AuthController: Forbidden/Unauthorized result
AuthController --> LoginScreen: HTTP 403/401 error
LoginScreen --> Guest: Show error message
else Account active
AuthService -> IAuthAccountRepository: StageLastLoginAsync(userId)
IAuthAccountRepository -> AuthAccountRepository: StageLastLoginAsync(userId)
AuthAccountRepository -> DbContext: Update User.LastLoginAt
DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE users
MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
AuthService -> IAuthAccountRepository: Create refresh token
IAuthAccountRepository -> AuthAccountRepository: Create refresh token
AuthAccountRepository -> RefreshTokenEntity: Create RefreshToken
RefreshTokenEntity --> AuthAccountRepository: RefreshToken
AuthAccountRepository -> DbContext: Add RefreshToken
DbContext -> MySQL: INSERT refresh_tokens
MySQL --> DbContext: Insert result
AuthService --> AuthController: Return login result
AuthController -> GoogleLoginResponseDto: Create response data(access_token, refresh_token,\nexpires_in, token_type)
AuthController -> FeTokensDto: HTTP 200 OK\nTokenResponse JSON
FeTokensDto --> LoginScreen: AuthTokens
LoginScreen --> Guest: Navigate to app
end
else New Google account
AuthService -> IAuthAccountRepository: FindByGoogleEmailAsync(email)
IAuthAccountRepository -> AuthAccountRepository: FindByGoogleEmailAsync(email)
AuthAccountRepository -> DbContext: Query user by Google email
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT user account
MySQL --> DbContext: User row or null
DbContext -> UserEntity: Materialize User?
DbContext -> UserAuthEntity: Materialize UserAuth?
UserEntity --> DbContext: User or null
UserAuthEntity --> DbContext: UserAuth or null
DbContext --> AuthAccountRepository: Result
AuthAccountRepository --> AuthService: AuthAccount or null
alt Google email already exists
AuthService --> AuthController: Conflict result
AuthController --> LoginScreen: HTTP 409 Google email already exists
LoginScreen --> Guest: Show error message
else Email is available
AuthService -> IAuthAccountRepository: FindRoleByNameAsync("User")
IAuthAccountRepository -> AuthAccountRepository: FindRoleByNameAsync("User")
AuthAccountRepository -> DbContext: Query role
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT roles
MySQL --> DbContext: Role row or null
DbContext -> RoleEntity: Materialize Role?
RoleEntity --> DbContext: Role or null
DbContext --> AuthAccountRepository: Result
AuthAccountRepository --> AuthService: AuthRole or null
alt Default user role missing
AuthService --> AuthController: Validation failure
AuthController --> LoginScreen: HTTP 400 error
LoginScreen --> Guest: Show error message
else Role exists
AuthService -> IAuthAccountRepository: StageCreateAsync(CreateAuthAccount)
IAuthAccountRepository -> AuthAccountRepository: StageCreateAsync(CreateAuthAccount)
AuthAccountRepository -> UserEntity: Create User
AuthAccountRepository -> UserAuthEntity: Create UserAuth
AuthAccountRepository -> UserProfileEntity: Create UserProfile
UserEntity --> AuthAccountRepository: User
UserAuthEntity --> AuthAccountRepository: UserAuth
UserProfileEntity --> AuthAccountRepository: UserProfile
AuthAccountRepository -> DbContext: Add User, UserAuth,\nUserProfile
DbContext -> MySQL: INSERT account data
MySQL --> DbContext: Insert result
DbContext --> AuthAccountRepository: Save result
AuthService -> IAuthAccountRepository: FindByGoogleSubjectAsync(subject)
IAuthAccountRepository -> AuthAccountRepository: FindByGoogleSubjectAsync(subject)
AuthAccountRepository -> DbContext: Reload created account
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT created user account
MySQL --> DbContext: Created user row
DbContext -> UserEntity: Materialize created User
DbContext -> UserAuthEntity: Materialize created UserAuth
DbContext -> UserProfileEntity: Materialize created UserProfile
UserEntity --> DbContext: User
UserAuthEntity --> DbContext: UserAuth
UserProfileEntity --> DbContext: UserProfile
DbContext --> AuthAccountRepository: Result
AuthAccountRepository --> AuthService: Created account
AuthService -> IAuthAccountRepository: Create refresh token
IAuthAccountRepository -> AuthAccountRepository: Create refresh token
AuthAccountRepository -> RefreshTokenEntity: Create RefreshToken
RefreshTokenEntity --> AuthAccountRepository: RefreshToken
AuthAccountRepository -> DbContext: Add RefreshToken
DbContext -> MySQL: INSERT refresh_tokens
MySQL --> DbContext: Insert result
DbContext --> AuthAccountRepository: Save result
AuthService --> AuthController: Return login result
AuthController -> GoogleLoginResponseDto: Create response data(access_token, refresh_token,\nexpires_in, token_type)
AuthController -> FeTokensDto: HTTP 200 OK\nTokenResponse JSON
FeTokensDto --> LoginScreen: AuthTokens
LoginScreen --> Guest: Navigate to app
end
end
end
end
end
end
@enduml
